      <h2>GF Wiki</h2>
      <p>
        This page explains the metrics Generation Football uses alongside
        traditional results: Expected Points (xPts), Elo ratings, the
        icons in player tables, and the abbreviations used in those tables.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="#xpoints">Expected Points (xPts)</a>
        ·
        <a href="#elo">Elo ratings</a>
        ·
        <a href="#player-icons">Player table icons</a>
        ·
        <a href="#abbreviations">Abbreviations</a>
      </p>

      <h2 id="xpoints">Expected Points (xPts)</h2>
      <p>
        Expected Points estimate how many points a team
        <em>deserved</em> from a match based on chance quality rather than the
        final score. A team that creates better chances can finish with a high
        xPts total even if the scoreboard does not go their way — and the
        reverse is also true.
      </p>
      <p>
        For each match we take the team’s expected goals (xG) and the
        opponent’s expected goals against them (xGA). We then use a Poisson
        probability model to estimate how likely every realistic scoreline is,
        treating each side’s goals as independent and considering totals from
        0 to 6 goals.
      </p>
      <p>
        Those scoreline probabilities add up to the chances of a win, a draw,
        or a loss. Expected Points are then:
        (win probability × 3) + (draw probability × 1).
      </p>
      <p>
        Season and last-five-match xPts figures are the sum of those match
        values. League tables are still ranked by real points; xPts is there
        to show which teams are over- or under-performing relative to the
        chances they created and conceded.
      </p>

      <h2 id="elo">Elo ratings</h2>
      <p>
        Elo is a running strength rating for teams. We keep
        <strong>club</strong> and <strong>national team</strong> ratings
        separate, so a club’s rating is not mixed with its country’s, and
        matches between clubs and national teams are skipped.
      </p>
      <p>
        Every team starts at 1500. Ratings use results from the last five
        seasons. Before a match we calculate how likely each side is to take
        points, using the classic Elo formula. Home teams get a +100 rating
        boost, except on designated neutral fixtures (World Cup, Euros and
        similar tournaments, plus club finals), where that advantage is 0.
      </p>
      <p>
        After the match, the result is scored as 1 for a win, 0.5 for a draw,
        and 0 for a loss. Penalty shootouts use the score after extra time, so
        they count as draws. A margin factor then scales the update: 1 for a
        draw or one-goal win, 1.5 for a two-goal win, and
        (11 + goal difference) / 8 for larger margins. The rating change is
        K × margin factor × (actual result − expected result).
      </p>
      <p>
        K depends on how important the match is: 20 for friendlies, 30 for
        domestic league and cup games, 40 for qualifiers and major club
        competitions, 50 for major national-team tournaments, and 60 for the
        World Cup final.
      </p>
      <p>
        On the site, club Elo is the tie-breaker on the
        <a href="/top-teams">Top Teams</a> list after recent form. Team pages
        show the last month of Elo movement, and match pages show how much
        each side gained or lost from that fixture.
      </p>

      <h2 id="player-icons">Player table icons</h2>
      <p>
        The <a href="/top-players">Top Players</a> table uses icons in the
        column headers. The same icons appear beside the matching statistic
        on a player’s page. Appearances, goals, assists, goals plus assists,
        and rating are on by default. The rest show when that statistic is
        switched on in the filters.
      </p>
      <ul class="wiki-icon-list">
        <li>
          {{> stat-icon name="apps"}}
          <span><strong>Appearances</strong> — matches the player has played in.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          {{> stat-icon name="goals"}}
          <span><strong>Goals</strong> — goals scored.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          {{> stat-icon name="assists"}}
          <span><strong>Assists</strong> — goals the player directly set up.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          {{> stat-icon name="ga"}}
          <span><strong>Goals + Assists</strong> — goals and assists added together.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          {{> stat-icon name="rating"}}
          <span><strong>Average rating</strong> — the player’s average match rating.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          {{> stat-icon name="minutes"}}
          <span><strong>Minutes</strong> — minutes played.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          {{> stat-icon name="pens"}}
          <span><strong>Penalties scored</strong> — penalties the player converted.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          {{> stat-icon name="penaltiesMissed"}}
          <span><strong>Penalties missed</strong> — penalties the player failed to score. The red line marks a miss.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          {{> stat-icon name="shotsOn"}}
          <span><strong>Shots on target</strong> — shots that were on goal.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="yellow-card"></span>
          <span><strong>Yellow cards</strong>.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="red-card"></span>
          <span><strong>Red cards</strong>.</span>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="abbreviations">Abbreviations</h2>
      <p>
        Short labels in table headers. Hovering a player-table header still
        shows the full name.
      </p>

      <h3>Players</h3>
      <ul class="wiki-abbr-list">
        <li><strong>NPG</strong> — non-penalty goals. Goals from open play, excluding penalties.</li>
        <li><strong>GA/90</strong> — goals plus assists per 90 minutes. Narrow screens show this as GA90.</li>
        <li><strong>No.</strong> — shirt number.</li>
        <li><strong>Sub Apps</strong> — substitute appearances.</li>
        <li><strong>Pens Won</strong> — penalties won.</li>
        <li><strong>Pens Com.</strong> — penalties committed.</li>
        <li><strong>Pens Saved</strong> — penalties saved by a goalkeeper.</li>
        <li><strong>Drib. Succ</strong> — successful dribbles.</li>
        <li><strong>Drib. Past</strong> — times an opponent dribbled past the player.</li>
        <li><strong>Acc. Passes</strong> — accurate passes.</li>
        <li><strong>Pass %</strong> — pass accuracy.</li>
        <li><strong>Interc.</strong> — interceptions.</li>
        <li><strong>GC</strong> — goals conceded.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>League and team tables</h3>
      <ul class="wiki-abbr-list">
        <li><strong>P</strong> — played.</li>
        <li><strong>W</strong> — wins.</li>
        <li><strong>D</strong> — draws.</li>
        <li><strong>L</strong> — losses.</li>
        <li><strong>GD</strong> — goal difference.</li>
        <li><strong>Pts</strong> — points.</li>
        <li><strong>Ag</strong> — against. Team tables pair this with For, for goals, expected goals, and the other split stats.</li>
        <li><strong>Rtg</strong> — rating, on match lineups.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Expected stats</h3>
      <ul class="wiki-abbr-list">
        <li><strong>xG</strong> — expected goals. The goals a team or player would be expected to score from the quality of the chances they had.</li>
        <li><strong>xGA</strong> — expected goals against. The same measure for chances conceded.</li>
        <li><strong>xGOT</strong> — expected goals on target. Expected goals from shots that were on target.</li>
        <li><strong>xA</strong> — expected assists.</li>
        <li><strong>xPts</strong> — expected points. How many points a team deserved from chance quality. See <a href="#xpoints">Expected Points</a>.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
